{
  "answer": "A primary key is a specific column or set of columns in a relational database table that uniquely identifies each record/row. Its main roles are to ensure data integrity by enforcing entity integrity (preventing duplicate rows) and to serve as the target for foreign keys to establish relationships between different tables.",
  "confidence": "high",
  "key_points": [
    "Uniquely identifies each record in a table",
    "Ensures entity integrity by prohibiting null and duplicate values",
    "Facilitates table relationships when referenced as a foreign key"
  ]
}

{
  "answer": "Gradient descent is an iterative optimization algorithm used to find the minimum of a function. Imagine you are standing on a foggy mountain and want to walk down to the lowest valley. You would feel the slope of the ground beneath your feet and take a step in the direction that slopes downward most steeply. By repeating this process of sensing the slope and taking a step, you will eventually reach the bottom of the valley. In machine learning, the mountain represents the model's error, and the steps are adjustments to the model's parameters to minimize that error.",
  "confidence": "high",
  "key_points": [
    "Iterative optimization algorithm used to minimize a function.",
    "Analogy of walking down a foggy mountain to the lowest valley.",
    "Calculates the slope (gradient) to determine the direction of the steepest descent.",
    "Used in machine learning to adjust model parameters and reduce error."
  ]
